item.text:
Source landscape: The 2023 documentary universe is broad and includes Thai government and parliamentary records, national statistics, NHSO and audit materials, UN/UNICEF/WHO/ILO/IOM sources, World Bank/OECD assessments, academic studies, and local-language civil-society research. Key source families cover social-protection design and financing, universal healthcare, education inequality, migrant and disability access, elderly welfare, public spending, poverty, and implementation gaps. Several records are post-period publications reporting 2023 conditions; these should be retained for later inspection with temporal fit assessed. Examples include the [World Bank inequality report](https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2023/11/29/focus-on-skills-education-regional-development-needed-to-create-a-more-equal-society-in-thailand), [UNICEF social-protection diagnostic](https://www.unicef.org/thailand/reports/thailand-social-protection-diagnostic-review-0), and [Thailand Statistical Yearbook 2023](https://www.nso.go.th/public/e-book/Statistical-Yearbook/SYB-2023/586/).

